    '|a||Unpaid harm gives too much. So what does an unpaid benefit give? Flu shots, with illustrative numbers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Demand is what people will pay to protect themselves. Supply is what it costs to make and give the shot.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:dza95w'
    '|b||Left alone, the market settles where they cross.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1h48hv8'
    '|a||But my shot protects more than me, doesn''t it? My grandmother, the bus driver, whoever I''d have coughed on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ai2ieq'
    '|b||It does. When Japan vaccinated its schoolchildren, one study estimated a death prevented for every four hundred and twenty children, mostly among the old.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:189ptl3'
    '|a||So a shot''s true value sits above what its buyer will pay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:c479yv'
    '|b||And true benefit meets supply further out. The town wants more shots than people buy for themselves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:g8r1fz'
    '|a||Then the gap is shots worth more than they cost, which nobody buys.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:o9883m'
    '|b||Too much of what harms bystanders, too little of what helps them. One cause: the price leaves them out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1can0g5'
    '|b||Hold on. When I buy a house, I push up prices for every other buyer. Isn''t that an externality? Shouldn''t I pay for it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||It feels like one. But follow the money: the other buyers lose, and the sellers gain exactly as much.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1pl83kk'
    '|a||That''s a pecuniary effect: it travels through a price. One side''s loss is the other''s gain, and nothing is wasted.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:9dtrgo'
    '|b||Whereas Mia''s ruined bread is nobody''s gain.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:l8h9um'
    '|a||Right. Only effects that skip the price make the market waste; economists call those technological externalities.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:w9dpf5'
    '|a||So ''it affects others'' isn''t enough. Nearly everything affects others. The test is whether a price carries it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1it78dq'
    '|a||How sure are we that unpriced harm is real? When E-ZPass cut idling at US toll plazas, premature births nearby fell by roughly seven to nine percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:8xfgjg'
    '|b||That markets overdo harm and underdo help is consensus. How big each gap is, and so what to do about it, is contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:rmknj'
    '|a||Now some new cases to try it on. Which kind of side effect is each? Sort the cards.':
